// The WRITTEN `impl Debug for Box`, in neither the declaring file nor the
// calling one. `12-derives-and-standard-interfaces/cross_file_debug` is the
// corpus program with exactly this orphan shape and it reaches it through the
// TYPE-qualified spelling (`Box.inspect`); main.nomi here reaches the same
// index entry through the INTERFACE-qualified one.
//
// Three files rather than two because the index needs BOTH a synthesized site
// and a written one under the same (receiver declaration, method) key, and a
// written impl in the DECLARING file suppresses the synthesis — measured, so
// the two shapes can only meet across a file boundary.
//
// `boxed` lives here rather than beside the struct so that main.nomi has a
// reason to import this file. A project is the import closure of its entry,
// and an impl block exports no name: with nothing imported from here the
// written block was simply absent from the program, and the fixture asserted
// the rule it was built to break.
import parts.Box

impl Debug for Box {
    fn inspect(x: Box): String {
        "written<" + Int.to_string(x.w) + ">"
    }
}

pub fn boxed(w: Int): Box {
    Box{w}
}
